cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "sharedstat: Diagnose and Correct Statistics Built from a Shared Component"
version: 0.1.0
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ruichen-bioinfo/sharedstat"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX      # uncomment and fill in after the first Zenodo release
# date-released: 2026-XX-XX        # fill in on the day of the release
abstract: >-
  Implements the two estimators, the attenuation result and the five admission checks described in the
  accompanying paper, together with a known-truth simulator in which compositionality emerges from
  closed-sum sampling rather than being imposed. Covers four constructions: a statistic formed against a
  shared reference arm, a residual correlated with its own component, a count of significant features read
  as an ordering of effect sizes, and an interaction contrast on compositional counts. Ranks no method as
  more accurate than another and describes no standard method as biased.
authors:
  - family-names: Chen
    given-names: Rui
    affiliation: Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München
keywords:
  - spurious correlation
  - shared component
  - measurement error
  - regression dilution
  - mathematical coupling
  - instrumental variable
  - compositional data
  - regulatory divergence
  - RNA-seq
  - reproducibility
